  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "For the SN 1278 pilot valve, corrosion bonding of the SRV pilot disc to the pilot seat likely caused the +3.8 percent out of tolerance as-found lift setpoint...an inherent problem with the Target Rock two-stage SRV design...For the SN 1223 pilot valve, the -5 percent out of tolerance lift setpoint was likely a result of a combination of degraded pilot valve assembly sub-components...the set pressure spring was not a matched set with the spring follower which likely resulted in the spring repositioning after being lifted and contributed to the side-loading of the spring",
    "cause_code": "B",
    "category": "Design/Manufacturing/Installation",
    "theme": "SRV pilot valve design/assembly degradation (corrosion bonding; mismatched spring set)",
    "provisional": false
  },
